            <mxPoint x="-530" y="1589.97" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="-480" y="1539.97" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UerNysRuGrNKIbmbH3ka-93" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;Question 3&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="290" x="-850" y="1740" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UerNysRuGrNKIbmbH3ka-95" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Entity Integrity:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Every provider in the Centene network must be uniquely identifiable. We use a &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;92&quot;&gt;National Provider Identifier (NPI)&lt;/b&gt; or an internal &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;142&quot;&gt;Provider_ID&lt;/b&gt; as the Primary Key. Entity integrity ensures that this ID is never null and never duplicated.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;If two different doctors were assigned the same ID, or if a provider was entered without a unique ID, the system wouldn&#39;t know which doctor to pay for a surgery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;It guarantees that every record in the &quot;Providers&quot; table represents one distinct, real-world entity, ensuring accurate reporting and payment routing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="690" x="-770" y="1780" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UerNysRuGrNKIbmbH3ka-96" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Domain Integrity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;This restricts the type, format, and range of data that can be entered into a specific column.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;For a &quot;Claim_Amount&quot; field, domain integrity would mandate a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;70&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Decimal&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; data type and a constraint where the value must be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;129&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;gt; 0&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;. For a &quot;Provider_Specialty&quot; field, we might use a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;183&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Check Constraint&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; or a dropdown list (e.g., &#39;Cardiology&#39;, &#39;Pediatrics&#39;, &#39;General Practice&#39;) to prevent someone from entering &quot;N/A&quot; or a typo like &quot;Cardoligy.&quot;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;It ensures data consistency across millions of claims. As an analyst, this prevents &quot;garbage in, garbage out&quot; scenarios, making it much easier to aggregate costs by specialty without cleaning thousands of typos.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot;&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="690" x="-760" y="2040" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UerNysRuGrNKIbmbH3ka-97" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Referential Integrity:&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;This ensures that relationships between tables remain consistent. A value in a Foreign Key column must match an existing value in the Primary Key column of the related table.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;In the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;16&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Claims Table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;, there is a column for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;52&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Plan_ID&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;. Referential integrity ensures that you cannot submit a claim for a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;128&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Plan_ID&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; that doesn&#39;t actually exist in the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;171&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Insurance_Plans Table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;. Similarly, if we try to delete a Plan from the system, referential integrity would &quot;restrict&quot; that deletion if there are still active claims tied to it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;It prevents &quot;orphan records.&quot; Without it, we might have claims for insurance plans that don&#39;t exist, meaning the system would have no way to determine the coverage limits or co-pay amounts for that claim, leading to a total system failure during adjudication.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot;&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="690" x="-760" y="2320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
